  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (basis cash); proprietary funds on accrual (business_type measure net position from p13-14). beginning_cash/ending_cash are the governmental funds' Fund Balances beginning 501,970 / end 572,634 (p10), which the statement rolls forward; total governmental cash is 580,134 (566,222 bank + 13,912 county treasurer, p6) less 7,500 due to other funds. Governmental transfers: Total column shows transfers in 114,000 and out 0 (interfund 541 eliminated in Adjustments column); the 114,000 comes from the Electric Fund. Grant Loan Advances/Repayments (CDBG revolving loans) recorded as other_financing. Proprietary cash-flow statement (p15-16) not recorded (proprietary field is GAAP-only): operating 178,782, noncapital (112,128), capital (75,795), investing 36,118, cash 1,031,350 -> 1,058,327. Balance sheet: the government-wide Statement of Net Position page in the trim (p1) prints only net position (its asset page is not in the trim) and includes governmental capital assets, so the governmental funds balance sheet (p5-6) plus the proprietary statement of net position (p11-12) are used, totals computed. Detail: Schedule of Expenditures by fund (p19-20) for governmental funds (Keno Fund all zero); the budgetary comparison schedule (p17-18) is for the total primary government, so only its business-type disbursement lines (Electric, Solid Waste, Sewer, Water) are recorded; its revenue lines combine governmental and business-type funds and its governmental lines duplicate the expenditure schedule, so they are skipped; no per-fund printed total exists for the four business lines. Read pages 1-20 of 20"
